      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 9.24,
      "end": 16.32,
      "text": "Most of them only once, sadly. You often cut, fold or write on the components, and once you know the puzzles, the surprise is gone."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 19.59,
      "end": 25.54,
      "text": "Some are designed so you don't destroy anything, so you can pass them on to friends afterward. The box usually says so."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 29.55,
      "end": 33.44,
      "text": "A lot of groups do that. You play one, they play another, then you swap."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 41.722,
      "end": 48.562,
      "text": "They have difficulty ratings on the box, and a hint system if you get stuck. Start with an easy one, it's more fun when you finish."
